    "result_text": "All 282 tests pass, including the new `Cp19Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation by adding a new OfficeFloor pipeline step to the `POST /api/owners` endpoint.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreation.java`:\n- Logs to a dedicated logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`).\n- Records the authenticated user (from `SecurityContextHolder`), the new owner's id, and its membership number.\n- Reads the persisted owner via `@Val Owner`, so both the generated id and the assigned membership number are populated.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (`save.next \u2192 audit`, `audit.next \u2192 respond`), so the audit only fires after a successful, committed save and before the response.\n\nThe log line produced is e.g. `Owner created by user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11`, satisfying the `Cp19Tests` assertion that the AUDIT logger records the user and the new owner id.",
